.'" "The mention of the latter," he adds, "no doubt suggested that of the ambiguous term Carmel, which is both a proper name and an appellative." -- Ed ^FT535 "Ceux qui n'ont point honte de commettre leurs meschancetez devant tous;" -- "Those who are not ashamed to commit their acts of wickedness in presence of all." ^FT536 "Ceux qui se levoyent de matin pour mal faire;" -- "They who rose early to do evil." ^FT537 "Il dit aussi que le juste est renvers? sans raison;" -- "He says also, that the righteous man is overthrown without any good reason." ^FT538 Both of the above quotations are made inaccurately. The words of Jeremiah are, "He putteth his mouth in the dust," and of Micah, "They shall lay their hand upon their mouth." But while the Author, quoting from memory, has altered the words, the passages are exceedingly apposite to his purpose. -- Ed ^FT539 "Qu'ils peuvent savoir ce que nous faisons au monde;" -- "That they can know what we are doing in the world."

